      <activity id="c64c845b-de36-5001-97d9-5d6dccb589be" activityNameId="18823495-a7ff-5451-9fd3-c8d98d6ac0aa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, filter dust Al electrolysis, 0% water, to residual material landfill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, filter dust Al electrolysis, 0% water, to residual material landfill
Inventoried waste contains 100% filter dust, aluminium electrolysis; . waste composition (wet, in ppm): upper heating value 0.18 MJ/kg; lower heating value 0.18 MJ/kg; H2O n.a.; O 382240; H n.a.; C 115860; S n.a.; N n.a.; P 580; B n.a.; Cl n.a.; Br n.a.; F 90510; I n.a.; Ag n.a.; As n.a.; Ba n.a.; Cd n.a.; Co n.a.; Cr 50; Cu 570; Hg n.a.; Mn n.a.; Mo n.a.; Ni 510; Pb 390; Sb n.a.; Se n.a.; Sn n.a.; V 480; Zn 30; Be n.a.; Sc n.a.; Sr n.a.; Ti 390; Tl n.a.; W n.a.; Si 460; Fe 5450; Ca n.a.; Al 338200; K n.a.; Mg 900; Na 63080; Share of carbon in waste that is biogenic 0%. Additional solidification with 0.3999 kg of cement.;; UUID: 68b7ae3b-f314-454a-be8d-31cafd534114
Waste-specific short-term emissions to water from leachate. Long-term emissions from landfill to ground water. Expenditures for solidificalion with cement (user-specified option)
Location: Technology encountered in Switzerland in 2000. Landfill includes base seal and leachate collection system.
Technology: Swiss residual material landfill for polluted, inorganic waste. With base seal and leachate collection system. Recultivation after closure. 
Time period: Waste composition as given in literature reference, theoretical data or other source. Transfer coefficients from prospective model.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Landfill model based on observed leachate concentrations in literature. Extrapolated to 60'000 years heeding chemical characteristics. Initial waste composition from various literature sources. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: uncertainty of waste input composition data derived from generic formula GSD(c) = N*ln(c)+1. Mean long-term emissions are the emissions until the next glacial period occurs (in 60'000a) and the landfill is eroded. Maximal long-term emissions are the complete emissions of all landfilled material (except Cr). Minimal long-term emissions are derived implicitly from the mean and maximal values assuming a lognormal distribution.
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_68b7ae3b-f314-454a-be8d-31cafd534114.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
